---@field declaredRestrictedCategories? gcp.realtimebidding_v1.CreativeDeclaredRestrictedCategoriesItemEnumList All declared restricted categories for the ads that may be shown from this creative. Can be used to filter the response of the creatives.list method.
---@field video? gcp.realtimebidding_v1.VideoContent A video creative.
---@field renderUrl? string Deprecated: FLEDGE is no longer supported. See: https://privacysandbox.google.com/blog/update-on-plans-for-privacy-sandbox-technologies Experimental field that can be used during the [FLEDGE Origin Trial](/authorized-buyers/rtb/fledge-origin-trial). The URL to fetch an interest group ad used in [TURTLEDOVE on-device auction](https://github.com/WICG/turtledove/blob/main/FLEDGE.md#1-browsers-record-interest-groups"). This should be unique among all creatives for a given `accountId`. This URL should be the same as the URL returned by [generateBid()](https://github.com/WICG/turtledove/blob/main/FLEDGE.md#32-on-device-bidding).
---@field apiUpdateTime? string Output only. The last update timestamp of the creative through the API.
---@field adChoicesDestinationUrl? string The link to AdChoices destination page. This is only supported for native ads.
---@field creativeId? string Buyer-specific creative ID that references this creative in bid responses. This field is Ignored in update operations. Can be used to filter the response of the creatives.list method. The maximum length of the creative ID is 128 bytes.
---@field declaredVendorIds? gcp.realtimebidding_v1.IntegerList IDs for the declared ad technology vendors that may be used by this creative. See https://storage.googleapis.com/adx-rtb-dictionaries/vendors.txt for possible values. Can be used to filter the response of the creatives.list method.
---@field declaredClickThroughUrls? gcp.realtimebidding_v1.StringList The set of declared destination URLs for the creative. Can be used to filter the response of the creatives.list method.

