---@alias gcp.realtimebidding_v1.ListBiddersCreativesAdCategoryTaxonomyOverrideEnum "AD_CATEGORY_TAXONOMY_UNSPECIFIED"|"GOOGLE_AD_CATEGORY_TAXONOMY"|"IAB_CONTENT_1_0"|"IAB_CONTENT_2_2"

---@class gcp.realtimebidding_v1.ListBiddersCreativesRequest
---@field pageToken? string A token identifying a page of results the server should return. Typically, this is the value of ListCreativesResponse.nextPageToken returned from the previous call to the 'ListCreatives' method. Page tokens for continued pages are valid for up to five hours, counting from the call to 'ListCreatives' for the first page.
---@field filter? string Query string to filter creatives. If no filter is specified, all active creatives will be returned. Example: 'accountId=12345 AND (dealsStatus:DISAPPROVED AND disapprovalReason:UNACCEPTABLE_CONTENT) OR declaredAttributes:IS_COOKIE_TARGETED'
---@field pageSize? number Requested page size. The server may return fewer creatives than requested (due to timeout constraint) even if more are available through another call. If unspecified, server will pick an appropriate default. Acceptable values are 1 to 1000, inclusive.
---@field parent string Required. Name of the parent buyer that owns the creatives. The pattern for this resource is either `buyers/{buyerAccountId}` or `bidders/{bidderAccountId}`. For `buyers/{buyerAccountId}`, the `buyerAccountId` can be one of the following: 1. The ID of the buyer that is accessing their own creatives. 2. The ID of the child seat buyer under a bidder account. So for listing creatives pertaining to the child seat buyer (`456`) under bidder account (`123`), you would use the pattern: `buyers/456`. 3. The ID of the bidder itself. So for listing creatives pertaining to bidder (`123`), you would use `buyers/123`. If you want to access all creatives pertaining to both the bidder and all of its child seat accounts, you would use `bidders/{bidderAccountId}`, for example, for all creatives pertaining to bidder (`123`), use `bidders/123`.
---@field adCategoryTaxonomyOverride? gcp.realtimebidding_v1.ListBiddersCreativesAdCategoryTaxonomyOverrideEnum|string Optional. The category taxonomy to use for the response. Overrides the default category taxonomy for the bidder.
---@field view? gcp.realtimebidding_v1.ListBiddersCreativesViewEnum|string Controls the amount of information included in the response. By default only creativeServingDecision is included. To retrieve the entire creative resource (including the declared fields and the creative content) specify the view as "FULL".

---@alias gcp.realtimebidding_v1.ListBiddersCreativesViewEnum "CREATIVE_VIEW_UNSPECIFIED"|"SERVING_DECISION_ONLY"|"FULL"

---@class gcp.realtimebidding_v1.ListBiddersEndpointsRequest
---@field pageSize? number The maximum number of endpoints to return. If unspecified, at most 100 endpoints will be returned. The maximum value is 500; values above 500 will be coerced to 500.
---@field pageToken? string A token identifying a page of results the server should return. This value is received from a previous `ListEndpoints` call in ListEndpointsResponse.nextPageToken.
---@field parent string Required. Name of the bidder whose endpoints will be listed. Format: `bidders/{bidderAccountId}`

---@class gcp.realtimebidding_v1.ListBiddersPretargetingConfigsRequest
---@field pageToken? string A token identifying a page of results the server should return. This value is received from a previous `ListPretargetingConfigs` call in ListPretargetingConfigsResponse.nextPageToken.
---@field pageSize? number The maximum number of pretargeting configurations to return. If unspecified, at most 10 pretargeting configurations will be returned. The maximum value is 100; values above 100 will be coerced to 100.
---@field parent string Required. Name of the bidder whose pretargeting configurations will be listed. Format: bidders/{bidderAccountId}

---@class gcp.realtimebidding_v1.ListBiddersPublisherConnectionsRequest
---@field filter? string Query string to filter publisher connections. Connections can be filtered by `displayName`, `publisherPlatform`, and `biddingState`. If no filter is specified, all publisher connections will be returned. Example: 'displayName="Great Publisher*" AND publisherPlatform=ADMOB AND biddingState != PENDING' See https://google.aip.dev/160 for more information about filtering syntax.
---@field orderBy? string Order specification by which results should be sorted. If no sort order is specified, the results will be returned in alphabetic order based on the publisher's publisher code. Results can be sorted by `createTime`. Example: 'createTime DESC'.
---@field pageSize? number Requested page size. The server may return fewer results than requested (due to timeout constraint) even if more are available through another call. If unspecified, the server will pick an appropriate default. Acceptable values are 1 to 5000, inclusive.
---@field parent string Required. Name of the bidder for which publishers have initiated connections. The pattern for this resource is `bidders/{bidder}` where `{bidder}` represents the account ID of the bidder.
---@field pageToken? string A token identifying a page of results the server should return. Typically, this is the value of ListPublisherConnectionsResponse.nextPageToken returned from the previous call to the 'ListPublisherConnections' method.

---@class gcp.realtimebidding_v1.ListBiddersRequest
---@field pageToken? string A token identifying a page of results the server should return. This value is received from a previous `ListBidders` call in ListBiddersResponse.nextPageToken.
---@field pageSize? number The maximum number of bidders to return. If unspecified, at most 100 bidders will be returned. The maximum value is 500; values above 500 will be coerced to 500.

---A response containing bidders.
---@class gcp.realtimebidding_v1.ListBiddersResponse
---@field nextPageToken? string A token which can be passed to a subsequent call to the `ListBidders` method to retrieve the next page of results in ListBiddersRequest.pageToken.
---@field bidders? gcp.realtimebidding_v1.BidderList List of bidders.

---@alias gcp.realtimebidding_v1.ListBuyersCreativesAdCategoryTaxonomyOverrideEnum "AD_CATEGORY_TAXONOMY_UNSPECIFIED"|"GOOGLE_AD_CATEGORY_TAXONOMY"|"IAB_CONTENT_1_0"|"IAB_CONTENT_2_2"

---@class gcp.realtimebidding_v1.ListBuyersCreativesRequest
---@field adCategoryTaxonomyOverride? gcp.realtimebidding_v1.ListBuyersCreativesAdCategoryTaxonomyOverrideEnum|string Optional. The category taxonomy to use for the response. Overrides the default category taxonomy for the bidder.
---@field pageSize? number Requested page size. The server may return fewer creatives than requested (due to timeout constraint) even if more are available through another call. If unspecified, server will pick an appropriate default. Acceptable values are 1 to 1000, inclusive.
---@field pageToken? string A token identifying a page of results the server should return. Typically, this is the value of ListCreativesResponse.nextPageToken returned from the previous call to the 'ListCreatives' method. Page tokens for continued pages are valid for up to five hours, counting from the call to 'ListCreatives' for the first page.
---@field filter? string Query string to filter creatives. If no filter is specified, all active creatives will be returned. Example: 'accountId=12345 AND (dealsStatus:DISAPPROVED AND disapprovalReason:UNACCEPTABLE_CONTENT) OR declaredAttributes:IS_COOKIE_TARGETED'
---@field view? gcp.realtimebidding_v1.ListBuyersCreativesViewEnum|string Controls the amount of information included in the response. By default only creativeServingDecision is included. To retrieve the entire creative resource (including the declared fields and the creative content) specify the view as "FULL".
---@field parent string Required. Name of the parent buyer that owns the creatives. The pattern for this resource is either `buyers/{buyerAccountId}` or `bidders/{bidderAccountId}`. For `buyers/{buyerAccountId}`, the `buyerAccountId` can be one of the following: 1. The ID of the buyer that is accessing their own creatives. 2. The ID of the child seat buyer under a bidder account. So for listing creatives pertaining to the child seat buyer (`456`) under bidder account (`123`), you would use the pattern: `buyers/456`. 3. The ID of the bidder itself. So for listing creatives pertaining to bidder (`123`), you would use `buyers/123`. If you want to access all creatives pertaining to both the bidder and all of its child seat accounts, you would use `bidders/{bidderAccountId}`, for example, for all creatives pertaining to bidder (`123`), use `bidders/123`.

---@alias gcp.realtimebidding_v1.ListBuyersCreativesViewEnum "CREATIVE_VIEW_UNSPECIFIED"|"SERVING_DECISION_ONLY"|"FULL"

---@class gcp.realtimebidding_v1.ListBuyersRequest
---@field pageSize? number The maximum number of buyers to return. If unspecified, at most 100 buyers will be returned. The maximum value is 500; values above 500 will be coerced to 500.
---@field pageToken? string A token identifying a page of results the server should return. This value is received from a previous `ListBuyers` call in ListBuyersResponse.nextPageToken.

---A response containing buyer account information.
---@class gcp.realtimebidding_v1.ListBuyersResponse
---@field nextPageToken? string A token which can be passed to a subsequent call to the `ListBuyers` method to retrieve the next page of results in ListBuyersRequest.pageToken.
---@field buyers? gcp.realtimebidding_v1.BuyerList List of buyers.

---@class gcp.realtimebidding_v1.ListBuyersUserListsRequest
---@field pageSize? number The number of results to return per page.
---@field parent string Required. The name of the parent buyer for the user lists to be returned that must follow the pattern `buyers/{buyerAccountId}`, where `{buyerAccountId}` represents the account ID of the buyer who owns user lists. For a bidder accessing user lists on behalf of a child seat buyer , `{buyerAccountId}` should represent the account ID of the child seat buyer.
---@field pageToken? string Continuation page token as received from a previous response.

---A response for listing creatives.
---@class gcp.realtimebidding_v1.ListCreativesResponse
---@field nextPageToken? string A token to retrieve the next page of results. Pass this value in the ListCreativesRequest.pageToken field in the subsequent call to the `ListCreatives` method to retrieve the next page of results.
---@field creatives? gcp.realtimebidding_v1.CreativeList The list of creatives.

---A response containing bidder endpoints.
---@class gcp.realtimebidding_v1.ListEndpointsResponse
---@field nextPageToken? string A token which can be passed to a subsequent call to the `ListEndpoints` method to retrieve the next page of results in ListEndpointsRequest.pageToken.
---@field endpoints? gcp.realtimebidding_v1.EndpointList List of bidder endpoints.

---A response containing pretargeting configurations.
---@class gcp.realtimebidding_v1.ListPretargetingConfigsResponse
---@field nextPageToken? string A token which can be passed to a subsequent call to the `ListPretargetingConfigs` method to retrieve the next page of results in ListPretargetingConfigsRequest.pageToken.
---@field pretargetingConfigs? gcp.realtimebidding_v1.PretargetingConfigList List of pretargeting configurations.

---A response to a request for listing publisher connections.
---@class gcp.realtimebidding_v1.ListPublisherConnectionsResponse
---@field publisherConnections? gcp.realtimebidding_v1.PublisherConnectionList The list of publisher connections.
---@field nextPageToken? string A token to retrieve the next page of results. Pass this value in the ListPublisherConnectionsRequest.pageToken field in the subsequent call to the `ListPublisherConnections` method to retrieve the next page of results.

---The list user list response.
---@class gcp.realtimebidding_v1.ListUserListsResponse
---@field userLists? gcp.realtimebidding_v1.UserListList List of user lists from the search.
---@field nextPageToken? string The continuation page token to send back to the server in a subsequent request. Due to a currently known issue, it is recommended that the caller keep invoking the list method until the time a next page token is not returned, even if the result set is empty.

---Information about each media file in the VAST.
---@class gcp.realtimebidding_v1.MediaFile
---@field mimeType? gcp.realtimebidding_v1.MediaFileMimeTypeEnum|string The MIME type of this media file. Can be used to filter the response of the creatives.list method.
---@field bitrate? string Bitrate of the video file, in Kbps. Can be used to filter the response of the creatives.list method.

---@alias gcp.realtimebidding_v1.MediaFileList gcp.realtimebidding_v1.MediaFile[]

---@alias gcp.realtimebidding_v1.MediaFileMimeTypeEnum "VIDEO_MIME_TYPE_UNSPECIFIED"|"MIME_VIDEO_XFLV"|"MIME_VIDEO_WEBM"|"MIME_VIDEO_MP4"|"MIME_VIDEO_OGG"|"MIME_VIDEO_YT_HOSTED"|"MIME_VIDEO_X_MS_WMV"|"MIME_VIDEO_3GPP"|"MIME_VIDEO_MOV"|"MIME_APPLICATION_SWF"|"MIME_APPLICATION_SURVEY"|"MIME_APPLICATION_JAVASCRIPT"|"MIME_APPLICATION_SILVERLIGHT"|"MIME_APPLICATION_MPEGURL"|"MIME_APPLICATION_MPEGDASH"|"MIME_AUDIO_MP4A"|"MIME_AUDIO_MP3"|"MIME_AUDIO_OGG"

---Native content for a creative.
---@class gcp.realtimebidding_v1.NativeContent
---@field starRating? number The app rating in the app store. Must be in the range [0-5].
---@field body? string A long description of the ad.
---@field advertiserName? string The name of the advertiser or sponsor, to be displayed in the ad creative.
---@field clickTrackingUrl? string The URL to use for click tracking.
---@field videoVastXml? string The contents of a VAST document for a native video ad.
---@field clickLinkUrl? string The URL that the browser/SDK will load when the user clicks the ad.
---@field videoUrl? string The URL to fetch a native video ad.
---@field logo? gcp.realtimebidding_v1.Image A smaller image, for the advertiser's logo.
---@field callToAction? string A label for the button that the user is supposed to click.
---@field headline? string A short title for the ad.
---@field image? gcp.realtimebidding_v1.Image A large image.
---@field appIcon? gcp.realtimebidding_v1.Image The app icon, for app download ads.
---@field priceDisplayText? string The price of the promoted app including currency info.

---Generic targeting used for targeting dimensions that contain a list of included and excluded numeric IDs used in app, user list, geo, and vertical id targeting.
---@class gcp.realtimebidding_v1.NumericTargetingDimension
---@field includedIds? gcp.realtimebidding_v1.StringList The IDs included in a config.
---@field excludedIds? gcp.realtimebidding_v1.StringList The IDs excluded in a config.

---@class gcp.realtimebidding_v1.OpenBuyersUserListsRequest
---@field name string Required. The name of the user list to open. See UserList.name
---@field body? gcp.realtimebidding_v1.OpenUserListRequest Request body

---A request to open a specified user list.
---@class gcp.realtimebidding_v1.OpenUserListRequest

---@class gcp.realtimebidding_v1.PatchBiddersEndpointsRequest
---@field tradingLocation? gcp.realtimebidding_v1.EndpointTradingLocationEnum|string The trading location that bid requests should be sent from. See https://developers.google.com/authorized-buyers/rtb/peer-guide#trading-locations for further information.
---@field maximumQps? string The maximum number of queries per second allowed to be sent to this server.
---@field url? string Output only. The URL that bid requests should be sent to.
---@field bidProtocol? gcp.realtimebidding_v1.EndpointBidProtocolEnum|string The protocol that the bidder endpoint is using.
---@field updateMask? string Field mask to use for partial in-place updates.
---@field name string Output only. Name of the endpoint resource that must follow the pattern `bidders/{bidderAccountId}/endpoints/{endpointId}`, where {bidderAccountId} is the account ID of the bidder who operates this endpoint, and {endpointId} is a unique ID assigned by the server.

---@class gcp.realtimebidding_v1.PatchBiddersPretargetingConfigsRequest
---@field billingId? string Output only. The identifier that corresponds to this pretargeting config that helps buyers track and attribute their spend across their own arbitrary divisions. If a bid request matches more than one config, the buyer chooses which billing_id to attribute each of their bids.
---@field displayName? string The diplay name associated with this config. This name must be unique among all the pretargeting configs a bidder has.
---@field maximumQps? string The maximum QPS threshold for this config. The bidder should receive no more than this number of bid requests matching this config per second across all their bidding endpoints among all trading locations. Further information available at https://developers.google.com/authorized-buyers/rtb/peer-guide
---@field minimumViewabilityDecile? number The targeted minimum viewability decile, ranging in values [0, 10]. A value of 5 means that the config will only match adslots for which we predict at least 50% viewability. Values > 10 will be rounded down to 10. An unset value or a value of 0 indicates that bid requests will be sent regardless of viewability.
---@field includedUserIdTypes? gcp.realtimebidding_v1.PretargetingConfigIncludedUserIdTypesItemEnumList User identifier types included in this config. At least one of the user identifier types specified in this list must be available for the bid request to be sent.
---@field webTargeting? gcp.realtimebidding_v1.StringTargetingDimension Targeting on a subset of site inventory. If WEB is listed in included_environments, the specified targeting is applied. A maximum of 50,000 site URLs can be targeted. An unset value for targeting allows all web-based bid requests to be sent. Sites can either be targeting positively (bid requests will be sent only if the destination site is listed in the targeting dimension) or negatively (bid requests will be sent only if the destination site is not listed in the pretargeting config).
---@field interstitialTargeting? gcp.realtimebidding_v1.PretargetingConfigInterstitialTargetingEnum|string The interstitial targeting specified for this config. The unset value will allow bid requests to be sent regardless of whether they are for interstitials or not.
---@field includedCreativeDimensions? gcp.realtimebidding_v1.CreativeDimensionsList Creative dimensions included by this config. Only bid requests eligible for at least one of the specified creative dimensions will be sent. An unset value allows all bid requests to be sent, regardless of creative dimension.
---@field invalidGeoIds? gcp.realtimebidding_v1.StringList Output only. Existing included or excluded geos that are invalid. Previously targeted geos may become invalid due to privacy restrictions.
---@field userListTargeting? gcp.realtimebidding_v1.NumericTargetingDimension The remarketing lists included or excluded in this config as defined in UserList.
---@field state? gcp.realtimebidding_v1.PretargetingConfigStateEnum|string Output only. The state of this pretargeting config.
---@field appTargeting? gcp.realtimebidding_v1.AppTargeting Targeting on a subset of app inventory. If APP is listed in targeted_environments, the specified targeting is applied. A maximum of 30,000 app IDs can be targeted. An unset value for targeting allows all app-based bid requests to be sent. Apps can either be targeting positively (bid requests will be sent only if the destination app is listed in the targeting dimension) or negatively (bid requests will be sent only if the destination app is not listed in the targeting dimension).
---@field geoTargeting? gcp.realtimebidding_v1.NumericTargetingDimension The geos included or excluded in this config defined in https://storage.googleapis.com/adx-rtb-dictionaries/geo-table.csv
---@field includedMobileOperatingSystemIds? gcp.realtimebidding_v1.StringList The mobile operating systems included in this config as defined in https://storage.googleapis.com/adx-rtb-dictionaries/mobile-os.csv
---@field includedPlatforms? gcp.realtimebidding_v1.PretargetingConfigIncludedPlatformsItemEnumList The platforms included by this config. Bid requests for devices with the specified platform types will be sent. An unset value allows all bid requests to be sent, regardless of platform.
---@field verticalTargeting? gcp.realtimebidding_v1.NumericTargetingDimension The verticals included or excluded in this config as defined in https://developers.google.com/authorized-buyers/rtb/downloads/publisher-verticals
---@field includedEnvironments? gcp.realtimebidding_v1.PretargetingConfigIncludedEnvironmentsItemEnumList Environments that are being included. Bid requests will not be sent for a given environment if it is not included. Further restrictions can be applied to included environments to target only a subset of its inventory. An unset value includes all environments.
---@field allowedUserTargetingModes? gcp.realtimebidding_v1.PretargetingConfigAllowedUserTargetingModesItemEnumList Deprecated: The value of this field no longer has any effect. Targeting modes included by this config. A bid request must allow all the specified targeting modes. An unset value allows all bid requests to be sent, regardless of which targeting modes they allow.
---@field publisherTargeting? gcp.realtimebidding_v1.StringTargetingDimension Targeting on a subset of publisher inventory. Publishers can either be targeted positively (bid requests will be sent only if the publisher is listed in the targeting dimension) or negatively (bid requests will be sent only if the publisher is not listed in the targeting dimension). A maximum of 10,000 publisher IDs can be targeted. Publisher IDs are found in [ads.txt](https://iabtechlab.com/ads-txt/) / [app-ads.txt](https://iabtechlab.com/app-ads-txt/) and in bid requests in the `BidRequest.publisher_id` field on the [Google RTB protocol](https://developers.google.com/authorized-buyers/rtb/downloads/realtime-bidding-proto) or the `BidRequest.site.publisher.id` / `BidRequest.app.publisher.id` field on the [OpenRTB protocol](https://developers.google.com/authorized-buyers/rtb/downloads/openrtb-adx-proto). Publisher IDs will be returned in the order that they were entered.
---@field includedLanguages? gcp.realtimebidding_v1.StringList The languages included in this config, represented by their language code. See https://developers.google.com/adwords/api/docs/appendix/languagecodes.
---@field excludedContentLabelIds? gcp.realtimebidding_v1.StringList The sensitive content category label IDs excluded in this config. Bid requests for inventory with any of the specified content label IDs will not be sent. Refer to this file https://storage.googleapis.com/adx-rtb-dictionaries/content-labels.txt for category IDs.
---@field includedFormats? gcp.realtimebidding_v1.PretargetingConfigIncludedFormatsItemEnumList Creative formats included by this config. Only bid requests eligible for at least one of the specified creative formats will be sent. An unset value will allow all bid requests to be sent, regardless of format.
---@field name string Output only. Name of the pretargeting config that must follow the pattern `bidders/{bidder_account_id}/pretargetingConfigs/{config_id}`
---@field updateMask? string Field mask to use for partial in-place updates.

---@class gcp.realtimebidding_v1.PatchBuyersCreativesRequest
---@field dealIds? gcp.realtimebidding_v1.StringList Output only. IDs of all of the deals with which this creative has been used in bidding. Can be used to filter the response of the creatives.list method.
---@field agencyId? string The agency ID for this creative.
---@field advertiserName? string The name of the company being advertised in the creative. Can be used to filter the response of the creatives.list method.
---@field accountId? string Output only. ID of the buyer account that this creative is owned by. Can be used to filter the response of the creatives.list method with equality and inequality check.
---@field creativeServingDecision? gcp.realtimebidding_v1.CreativeServingDecision Output only. Top level status and detected attributes of a creative (for example domain, language, advertiser, product category, etc.) that affect whether (status) and where (context) a creative will be allowed to serve.
---@field html? gcp.realtimebidding_v1.HtmlContent An HTML creative.
---@field version? number Output only. The version of the creative. Version for a new creative is 1 and it increments during subsequent creative updates.
---@field declaredAttributes? gcp.realtimebidding_v1.CreativeDeclaredAttributesItemEnumList All declared attributes for the ads that may be shown from this creative. Can be used to filter the response of the creatives.list method. If the `excluded_attribute` field of a [bid request](https://developers.google.com/authorized-buyers/rtb/downloads/realtime-bidding-proto") contains one of the attributes that were declared or detected for a given creative, and a bid is submitted with that creative, the bid will be filtered before the auction.
---@field restrictedCategories? gcp.realtimebidding_v1.CreativeRestrictedCategoriesItemEnumList All restricted categories for the ads that may be shown from this creative.
---@field impressionTrackingUrls? gcp.realtimebidding_v1.StringList The set of URLs to be called to record an impression.
---@field creativeFormat? gcp.realtimebidding_v1.CreativeCreativeFormatEnum|string Output only. The format of this creative. Can be used to filter the response of the creatives.list method.
---@field native? gcp.realtimebidding_v1.NativeContent A native creative.
---@field declaredRestrictedCategories? gcp.realtimebidding_v1.CreativeDeclaredRestrictedCategoriesItemEnumList All declared restricted categories for the ads that may be shown from this creative. Can be used to filter the response of the creatives.list method.
---@field video? gcp.realtimebidding_v1.VideoContent A video creative.
---@field renderUrl? string Deprecated: FLEDGE is no longer supported. See: https://privacysandbox.google.com/blog/update-on-plans-for-privacy-sandbox-technologies Experimental field that can be used during the [FLEDGE Origin Trial](/authorized-buyers/rtb/fledge-origin-trial). The URL to fetch an interest group ad used in [TURTLEDOVE on-device auction](https://github.com/WICG/turtledove/blob/main/FLEDGE.md#1-browsers-record-interest-groups"). This should be unique among all creatives for a given `accountId`. This URL should be the same as the URL returned by [generateBid()](https://github.com/WICG/turtledove/blob/main/FLEDGE.md#32-on-device-bidding).
---@field apiUpdateTime? string Output only. The last update timestamp of the creative through the API.
---@field adChoicesDestinationUrl? string The link to AdChoices destination page. This is only supported for native ads.
---@field creativeId? string Buyer-specific creative ID that references this creative in bid responses. This field is Ignored in update operations. Can be used to filter the response of the creatives.list method. The maximum length of the creative ID is 128 bytes.
---@field declaredVendorIds? gcp.realtimebidding_v1.IntegerList IDs for the declared ad technology vendors that may be used by this creative. See https://storage.googleapis.com/adx-rtb-dictionaries/vendors.txt for possible values. Can be used to filter the response of the creatives.list method.
---@field declaredClickThroughUrls? gcp.realtimebidding_v1.StringList The set of declared destination URLs for the creative. Can be used to filter the response of the creatives.list method.
---@field name string Output only. Name of the creative. Follows the pattern `buyers/{buyer}/creatives/{creative}`, where `{buyer}` represents the account ID of the buyer who owns the creative, and `{creative}` is the buyer-specific creative ID that references this creative in the bid response.
---@field updateMask? string Field mask to use for partial in-place updates.

---Policy compliance of the creative for a transaction type or a region.
---@class gcp.realtimebidding_v1.PolicyCompliance
---@field status? gcp.realtimebidding_v1.PolicyComplianceStatusEnum|string Serving status for the given transaction type (for example, open auction, deals) or region (for example, China, Russia). Can be used to filter the response of the creatives.list method.
---@field topics? gcp.realtimebidding_v1.PolicyTopicEntryList Topics related to the policy compliance for this transaction type (for example, open auction, deals) or region (for example, China, Russia). Topics may be present only if status is DISAPPROVED.

---@alias gcp.realtimebidding_v1.PolicyComplianceStatusEnum "STATUS_UNSPECIFIED"|"PENDING_REVIEW"|"DISAPPROVED"|"APPROVED"|"CERTIFICATE_REQUIRED"

---Each policy topic entry will represent a violation of a policy topic for a creative, with the policy topic information and optional evidence for the policy violation.
---@class gcp.realtimebidding_v1.PolicyTopicEntry
---@field evidences? gcp.realtimebidding_v1.PolicyTopicEvidenceList Pieces of evidence associated with this policy topic entry.
---@field missingCertificate? boolean Whether or not the policy topic is missing a certificate.
---@field helpCenterUrl? string URL of the help center article describing this policy topic.
---@field policyTopic? string Policy topic this entry refers to. For example, "ALCOHOL", "TRADEMARKS_IN_AD_TEXT", or "DESTINATION_NOT_WORKING". The set of possible policy topics is not fixed for a particular API version and may change at any time. Can be used to filter the response of the creatives.list method

---@alias gcp.realtimebidding_v1.PolicyTopicEntryList gcp.realtimebidding_v1.PolicyTopicEntry[]

---Evidence associated with a policy topic entry.
---@class gcp.realtimebidding_v1.PolicyTopicEvidence
---@field downloadSize? gcp.realtimebidding_v1.DownloadSizeEvidence Total download size and URL-level download size breakdown for resources in a creative.
---@field destinationNotCrawlable? gcp.realtimebidding_v1.DestinationNotCrawlableEvidence The creative's destination URL was not crawlable by Google.
---@field destinationUrl? gcp.realtimebidding_v1.DestinationUrlEvidence URL of the actual landing page.
---@field httpCall? gcp.realtimebidding_v1.HttpCallEvidence HTTP calls made by the creative that resulted in policy violations.
---@field destinationNotWorking? gcp.realtimebidding_v1.DestinationNotWorkingEvidence The creative's destination URL did not function properly or was incorrectly set up.
---@field httpCookie? gcp.realtimebidding_v1.HttpCookieEvidence Evidence for HTTP cookie-related policy violations.
---@field domainCall? gcp.realtimebidding_v1.DomainCallEvidence Number of HTTP calls made by the creative, broken down by domain.

---@alias gcp.realtimebidding_v1.PolicyTopicEvidenceList gcp.realtimebidding_v1.PolicyTopicEvidence[]

